  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: Unnumbered Site Location Plan, Unnumbered Existing Block Plan, Unnumbered Proposed Block Plan, PA 01, PA 02, PA 03, PA 04. Received: 25th February 2025.\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - The windows formed in the eastern side dormer and western roof slope shall be obscure-glazed and non-opening below 1.7 metres above internal floor level. The windows shall not be repaired or replaced otherwise than in accordance with the requirements of this condition. Reason: In order to protect neighbours' privacy",
    "Condition : 5 - The roof light window to be fitted on the side roof face of the dwelling shall be black-framed and traditional, conservation-style.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the architectural and historic interest of the conservation area."
